      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T04:31:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/blueprint/transition.go;l\u003d23;drc\u003d04ca6dc70ff1d021796faa7db90b05f54295d58c for how transition mutators work.  `Split` implements the variants that should be created for the module based solely on its own properties, and then additional variants can be created from incoming dependencies via the `OutgoingTransition` and `IncomingTransition` methods.\n\nIn this case, no modules get any variations based on their own properties, because we only use the `\"sabi\"` variation for static dependencies, the top level shared library that enables sabi still uses the `\"\"` variation.\n\n`\"\"` doesn\u0027t skip anything, it still calls `OutgoingTransition` for outgoing dependencies, and it still calls `Mutate` with `\"\"` as the variation.",
      "parentUuid": "a1c496b8_835c7c4a",
      "range": {
