      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. So the `\"\"` variation is like the \"default\" variant we used to have?\n\nSo for the top-level shared library module, the dep graph would become:\n\n```\nlibshared (variation: {\"sabi\": \"\"}) -\u003e libstatic (variation: {\"sabi\": \"sabi\"})\n```\n\nboth the \"normal\" cc linking and header-abi-linker is called with artifacts coming from the `{\"sabi\": \"sabi\"}`-variation dependency right?\n\n\nIf libshared doesn\u0027t want to use sabi:\n```\nlibshared (variation: {\"sabi\": \"\"}) -\u003e libstatic (variation: {\"sabi\": \"\"})\n```\nAnd this is what you meant that some static lib modules could be compiled twice?",
